--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCEPTION: THE WEB CLIENT IS APACHE-2.0

Everything under web/ is licensed separately, under the Apache License 2.0 —
see web/LICENSE. Fork it, change it, ship your own client.

The split is deliberate. A forked CLIENT talks to these same contracts and the
same people, so more clients make one network stronger. Forked CONTRACTS would
be a second network wearing the same name, which helps nobody. Hence: the client
is open, the contracts are readable.

Apache-2.0 section 6 grants no trademark rights, and we rely on it: fork the
client freely, but call it something other than Platho.
